In article <1992Mar4.181226.18941@math.utexas.edu>, heinz@wombat.ma.utexas.edu (Martin Heinz) writes:
> Also, BTW- How come you killed the Wiz and still don't have the AoY???

Now that, my friend, is an outstanding question.  This was my first
trip into hell, and I didn't know what to expect.  When I first found
the Wizard, he scooped up the amulet, and when I killed him, I thought
I picked it up and put it into an uncursed bag I was carrying (yeah,
I'd heard that was impossible, too), and since I hit a teleport trap
shortly thereafter, I took off my magic resisting cloak and teleported
to level 1.

The game told me I felt vaguely nervous.  No joke, I say to myself.  So
I check the bag-- no amulet (???).  Confused, I went back to dungeon
level 50, and rechecked every single square in hell until I got back to
where I teleported out.  And I checked Vlad's tower (I thought there
were supposed to be three of them, but I only found one).  No amulet.
And although I killed the Wizard at least a dozen times, the only other
Amulet of Yendor I found went into my bag.

I concluded that the wizard must have done some sort of switcheroo.  If
I had lived long enough, I intended to find some way to identify the
rings I was carrying (I knew one of them was teleport control, because
it came from one of my own bones files).  I figured when I got out of
hell, I'd try to polymorph into a nymph and steal it from the Wizard.
But I never lived to solve the mystery.

